        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 1:52AM EDT until September 25 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, northeast winds 30 to 35 kt with
gusts up to 40 kt and seas 13 to 15 ft. For the Storm Warning,
north winds 35 to 45 kt with gusts up to 60 kt and seas 17 to
22 ft expected.

* WHERE...Waters from Sandy Hook NJ to Manasquan Inlet NJ from
20 to 40 NM, Waters from Manasquan Inlet NJ to Little Egg
Inlet NJ from 20 to 60 NM, Waters from Little Egg Inlet NJ to
Great Egg Inlet NJ from 20 to 60 NM and Waters from Great Egg
Inlet NJ to Cape May NJ from 20 to 60 NM.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 AM EDT early this
morning. For the Storm Warning, from 6 AM this morning to 6 AM
EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Storm force winds and hazardous seas will capsize or
damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should remain in port, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
